{"title":"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Efficient)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Efficient)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Linearity_of_Expectation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Linearity of Expectation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Johann has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> fair coins. He flips all the coins. Any coin that lands on tails is tossed again. Coins that land on tails on the second toss are tossed a third time. What is the expected number of coins that are now heads?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb6e54858e5d3f16faa84237979d4d094f5855e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 32 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 40 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 48 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 56 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can simplify the problem first, then apply reasoning to the original problem. Let's say that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> coins. Shaded coins flip heads, and blank coins flip tails. So, after the first flip;\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/a/3dac3cb762d73e6a8d3b8ec7c535a5096bb79831.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] filldraw(circle((-5,0),0.35),white); filldraw(circle((-4,0),0.35),white); filldraw(circle((-3,0),0.35),white); filldraw(circle((-2,0),0.35),white); filldraw(circle((-1,0),0.35),black); filldraw(circle((-0,0),0.35),black); filldraw(circle((1,0),0.35),black); filldraw(circle((2,0),0.35),black); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>Then, after the second (new heads in blue);\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/8/688ee107045ce8085b5b481a7c8405dea7edbd7c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] filldraw(circle((-5,0),0.35),white); filldraw(circle((-4,0),0.35),white); filldraw(circle((-3,0),0.35),blue); filldraw(circle((-2,0),0.35),blue); filldraw(circle((-1,0),0.35),black); filldraw(circle((-0,0),0.35),black); filldraw(circle((1,0),0.35),black); filldraw(circle((2,0),0.35),black); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>And after the third (new head in green);\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/1/49134c0babdbc3bc848608ad22e9888c3d851db6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] filldraw(circle((-5,0),0.35),white); filldraw(circle((-4,0),0.35),green); filldraw(circle((-3,0),0.35),blue); filldraw(circle((-2,0),0.35),blue); filldraw(circle((-1,0),0.35),black); filldraw(circle((-0,0),0.35),black); filldraw(circle((1,0),0.35),black); filldraw(circle((2,0),0.35),black); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>So in total, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> coins resulted in heads. Now we have the ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/7/717366d5cd3f9573014d073ca33467c37c12a364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of the total coins will end up heads. Therefore, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/128085102a982ed75c2d4968eddf4b0de1c427b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{8}\\cdot64=\\boxed{\\mathbf{(D)}\\ 56}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"134\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Efficient.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Efficient)\">Solution 2 (Efficient)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Efficient)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Every time the coins are flipped, half of them are expected to turn up heads. The expected number of heads on the first flip is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, on the second flip is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and on the third flip, it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Adding these gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bce28b048907be23eab8f2cc3c098cd4994aa3a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathbf{(D)}\\ 56}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"29\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Every time the coins are flipped, each of them has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3cc0ad966b3e637cd199607cbf0d1befc0e491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" /> probability of being tails. Doing this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/6136193afb3f1957d9feaa1b626ccc1e01eed6f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> of them will be tails. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e07d569cbf6cb0372e4447d2fe939573d060475b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64-64*1/8=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bce28b048907be23eab8f2cc3c098cd4994aa3a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathbf{(D)}\\ 56}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p>~Lcz\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(Similar to solution 2)\n</p><p>Notice how:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07dfb31b86ef271aa8a2bafd6719df2e03e0e245.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(\\text{Heads on 1st flip, 2nd flip, 3rd flip}) = E(\\text{Heads on 1st flip}) + E(\\text{Heads on 2nd flip}) + E(\\text{Heads on 3rd flip})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"811\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>The expected number of heads for the first flip is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/2/892f229dd7504b8b307efaa7c9ad8512df97901f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"38\" />, since each coin has a 1 in 2 chance of being heads. Then, we are left with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b59b7554d4fbd2d1fb8bfc52111b0a2117bfdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64 - 32 = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> coins. Then, half of these coins will be heads again, which leaves us with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/4/9446abedff6a73beb9f2fb4adba52330d4ecd2ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32 - 16 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> coins. Then, half of these coins will be heads again, which leaves us with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/79385e36cbdd40fddb61e694e28fa6dc02f57c2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 - 8 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> coins.\n</p><p>Hence, the expected number of heads is simply:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfedf902c162668d1ac508fc8594eea7b7dda904.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32 + 16 + 8 = \\boxed{56} \\implies D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"210\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~yk2007\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Linearity_of_Expectation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Linearity_of_Expectation)\">Solution 5 (Linearity of Expectation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Linearity of Expectation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As you may have guessed from the title, we will be using Linearity of Expectation to solve this problem. We will first look at the expected value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> coin, then multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> at the end, since expected value is linear. First, you can almost imagine, a markov chain or a tree chart. We first have a coin, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> outcomes, heads and tails For heads, there is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/4/4a4a7df1100efe353cc612d5d1c289c22d5bf8c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> chance of flipping one, and we multiply it by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> since we got <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> head to come out. Now, lets look at the outcome where we get a tail on the first roll. We just roll, again, so the probability of getting a heads on the second roll is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/9/5795f6a5b12806b0e0b5a1d1bbc3cf4522cd321c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{2} = \\dfrac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" />. Again, we multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for the same reason. Now, same thing for the third roll it would just be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/6273fe54147794e9bc70f0d62d642da0102edd4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{8} \\cdot 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"37\" height=\"38\" />. Summing it all up we get: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/8/b1855fc555b6fdf146d6e61562768ac3440576dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{1}{2} + \\dfrac{1}{4} + \\dfrac{1}{8} = \\dfrac{7}{8} \\cdot 64 = \\boxed{\\mathbf{(D)\\ 56}}\\]\" width=\"243\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\n~jb2015007\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0uCMSH7-Ubk\">https://youtu.be/0uCMSH7-Ubk</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B\">2015 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>